In C, the constant `N` is 4096 and a is a rectangular array of eight-byte doubles. Which loop has the contiguous inner access pattern and fewer demand misses in the lesson's cold aligned 64-byte-line, 32 KiB fully associative LRU model, with no prefetching or other accesses?

```c
// A: use neighbouring doubles together.
for (i = 0; i < N; i++)
  for (j = 0; j < N; j++)
    s += a[i][j];
// B: next read is in another row.
for (j = 0; j < N; j++)
  for (i = 0; i < N; i++)
    s += a[i][j];
```
